# The paths below leave every `git archive` of this repository, and so leave
# `dist`, the branch the plugin directory reads, whose tree at each release
# is the archive of the release's tag. They are this repository's own
# development: its suites, its records, what only a contributor's session
# reads, its own workflows, and the scripts under `.github/scripts/` that
# only those workflows run. The workflows also leave because GitHub
# refuses a push made with a workflow's own token that creates or changes a
# file under `.github/workflows/`, so a `dist` commit holding them would
# never be pushed; no installed copy runs them. A script under
# `.github/scripts/` leaves by its own line, because three there stay: a
# shipped command runs each, as `docs/releasing/branch-and-release.md`
# *The plugin directory reads `dist`* says. This file lists what leaves
# and not what stays, because a path forgotten here reaches `dist` and costs
# size or a directory finding, where a path forgotten in a list of what
# stays would be missing from every copy the directory serves with nothing
# in this repository to show it. A pull request that adds a path only
# development reads adds its line here.
/tests/ export-ignore
/evals/ export-ignore
/seal/ export-ignore
/.test_durations export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/.github/workflows/ export-ignore
/.github/scripts/dist_branch.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/durations_union.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/finding_counts.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/issue_claims_check.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/label_merged_on_release_branch.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/plugin_directory_check.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/publish_release_note.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/release_completeness_check.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/release_report.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/release_seal.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/roll_flow_measurement_issue.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/tag_release.py export-ignore
/.github/scripts/tracker_labels.py export-ignore
